{"id":"n-20261013-s4432b","category":"finance","display_title":"Tragic School Trip Explosion","display_title_he":"אסון הפיצוץ בטיול בית הספר","short_summary":"An unexploded ordnances tragedy during a school trip at Ramim Ridge raises critical legal and compensation questions.","english_level":"C1","words":484,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Susette_Schultz_Keast_-_c4f4f6d8a5.jpg/960px-Susette_Schultz_Keast_-_c4f4f6d8a5.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Susette Schultz Keast · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Susette_Schultz_Keast_-_c4f4f6d8a5.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3871993","title":"אסון הנפל בטיול: מי יפצה את משפחות הנפגעים - וכמה כסף מגיע להן?","published_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-13T09:41:12.545Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["A tragic incident recently shook the community at Ramim Ridge, where an unexploded munition detonated during a school excursion. The blast resulted in the death of fourteen-year-old Elazar Yair and left more than twenty other individuals injured. According to initial assessments provided by the Israel Defense Forces, the dangerous object was a remnant of a Hezbollah cluster bomb left behind in the field.","Following the disaster, complex legal and financial questions have emerged regarding compensation for the victims and their families. Insurance and tort law experts note that injuries stemming from hostile enemy weapons can typically be recognized as hostile act casualties. This classification depends on the intended purpose of the weapon rather than the specific manner in which it detonated. Consequently, formal claims are expected to be submitted to the National Insurance Institute, with final determinations made by the authorizing body within the Ministry of Defense.","Preliminary security checks raised questions regarding whether a student was carrying the unexploded device in a backpack prior to the explosion. Legal specialists clarify that even if this claim is substantiated, it should not jeopardize the victims' eligibility for state recognition. Statutory restrictions regarding illegal actions generally apply to adults committing intentional crimes or gross negligence, whereas the students involved are minors. Furthermore, authorities have not raised similar allegations against the accompanying teachers, and the backpack claim remains unverified.","Once an incident receives official recognition as a hostile act, the National Insurance Institute becomes responsible for financial compensation. Parents must submit specific claims, after which medical committees will assess each student's permanent disability percentage. Disability ratings below ten percent do not yield financial grants, while ranges between ten and nineteen percent qualify for a one-time grant. For disabilities reaching twenty percent or higher, a monthly stipend is awarded, which can reach approximately 5,800 shekels for complete disability.","Additional legal scrutiny surrounds potential liability on the part of the Ministry of Education and the school management. Plaintiffs may pursue negligence claims, arguing that educational institutions owe a heightened duty of care to students, particularly during outdoor trips. Student testimonies suggest that no warnings were given regarding suspicious objects, and some claimed the device was handled for over an hour. Conversely, defense arguments are likely to rely on the fact that the Ministry's situation room approved the route in coordination with security officials, though it remains unclear if the exact path matched the official authorization.","Standard student personal accident insurance policies provide broad round-the-clock coverage, but they explicitly exclude injuries resulting from hostile acts, war, or military operations. Therefore, because the source of the blast was enemy ordnance, standard accident policies will not cover the incident. Meanwhile, claims for lost or damaged personal equipment must be directed to the Property Tax compensation fund operated by the Tax Authority. This fund covers war-related damages, though officials warn that proven negligence by the claimant could potentially reduce or invalidate the compensation award."],"facts":[{"fact":"A tragic explosion occurred at Ramim Ridge, resulting in the death of 14-year-old Elazar Yair and injuring more than 20 people.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"According to the IDF, the explosion was caused by an unexploded Hezbollah cluster bomb remnant.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Legal experts explain that compensation claims can be filed through the National Insurance Institute for hostile act injuries, and via civil negligence claims against the Ministry of Education and school management.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Property damage, such as personal equipment, can be claimed through the Tax Authority's Property Tax compensation fund.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Tragic School Trip Explosion","lemma":"tragic school trip explosion","pos":"name","he":"אסון הפיצוץ בטיול בית הספר","name":true},{"text":"Ramim Ridge","lemma":"ramim ridge","pos":"name","he":"רכס רמים","name":true},{"text":"Elazar Yair","lemma":"elazar yair","pos":"name","he":"אלעזר יאיר","name":true},{"text":"Israel Defense Forces","lemma":"israel defense forces","pos":"name","he":"צבא ההגנה לישראל","name":true},{"text":"Hezbollah","lemma":"hezbollah","pos":"name","he":"חזבאללה","name":true},{"text":"National Insurance Institute","lemma":"national insurance institute","pos":"name","he":"המוסד לביטוח לאומי","name":true},{"text":"Ministry of Defense","lemma":"ministry of defense","pos":"name","he":"משרד הביטחון","name":true},{"t